    <string name="skiptab_why_title">Why some ads can\'t be skipped</string>
    <string name="skiptab_why_content">1. Countdown lock: some ad SDKs swallow every tap during the countdown — accessibility clicks, gestures, even the back key do nothing. That\'s by the advertiser\'s design.\n2. Shake-to-open ads: triggered by the motion sensor, which Android doesn\'t let one app block for another. We close them as fast as we can.\n3. Buttons baked into images: some "skip" buttons are drawn into an image with no real button in the system tree, so we can only guess the usual top-right spot.\nWhen any of this happens, the diagnostic log records it truthfully — the service did its job; the advertiser blocked the way.</string>
    <string name="skiptab_stats">Skipped today: %1$d · Total: %2$d</string>
    <string name="skiptab_app_list">Boost Apps</string>
    <string name="app_list_title">Boost Apps</string>
    <string name="app_list_note">When enabled, the service tries harder to skip splash ads for that app (taps the top-right blind spot if no skip button is found)</string>
    <string name="app_list_all_on">Boost All</string>
    <string name="app_list_all_off">Unboost All</string>
    <string name="app_list_search_hint">Search apps</string>
    <string name="skiptab_help">How to use:\n1. Tap the button above to open the system\'s Accessibility settings\n2. Find \"TiaoYiTiao\" and turn it on\n3. When a splash ad appears in other apps, it will auto-tap \"Skip\"\n\nNote: it only taps the ad\'s own Skip button — nothing is read or uploaded. You can turn it off in system settings anytime.\nA persistent \"Skip Ads Running\" notification appears after enabling (prevents the service from being killed when clearing background apps; Android requires this — long-press to silence it).\n\nIf the toggle turns off after clearing background apps / the service doesn\'t start after reboot:\n%1$s</string>
